('140','YONA','The word Yona in Pali and the Prakrits, and the analogue Yavana in Sanskrit, were used in Ancient India to designate Greek speakers. "Yona" and "Yavana" are transliterations of the Greek word for "Ionians", who were probably the first Greeks to be known in India.','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yona','2026-05-18 23:38:12','2026-05-18 23:18:39','2026-05-18 23:38:12'),
